+## Current activation (momentum cost-sensitivity check; signal-definition defect — run 43956531905, agent 02, task R-001)
+
+Ran a bounded, predeclared transaction-cost sensitivity check of the qualified
+momentum edge (task R-001) and, in the process, found that the momentum signal
+does not implement the momentum rule its docstring states.
+
+**Signal-definition finding (material, decision-relevant).** In
+`research/backtest/regime_stability.py`, `momentum_signals` computes
+
+    ret = float(np.mean(np.log(closes[i - lookback + 1 : i + 1])))
+
+i.e. the **mean log PRICE level** over the window (not the lookback RETURN), and
+sets weight = +1 iff that mean log price > 0. For the collected large caps the
+price level is essentially always above $1, so the signal is a **static long**:
+
+- 9/10 tickers are constant-long (+1 on every active bar) at lookbacks 3/5/10,
+  with **0 active sign flips**; NVDA is the only exception (one active flip where
+  its split-adjusted price was below $1 early in the sample).
+- The signal equals the price-level threshold rule for **all 10 tickers × 3
+  lookbacks** (`all_match_price_level_rule=True`), while its agreement with the
+  intended lookback-return sign `sign(log(closes[i]) - log(closes[i-lookback]))`
+  is only **~0.54–0.60** (chance). The implementation therefore carries no
+  momentum information; it is a level/static-long bet.
+- This also explains the prior activation's "horizon-stable in magnitude"
+  result (identical medians across lookbacks 3/5/10/20/60): the lookback only
+  shifts a few warmup bars, so the position is unchanged.
+
+**Cost-sensitivity grid (predeclared, on the existing implementation).**
+Lookbacks {3,5,10} × cost {zero, realistic (the repo's canonical model:
+commission_per_trade=2.0, commission_per_share=0.003, slippage_cents=2.0,
+slippage_proportional=0.0005), stress2x (all cost parameters doubled)}, each run
+through `stress_segments_across_tickers` with the matched coin-flip null on the
+10-asset universe (manifest 10/10, preflight PASSED, leakage PASS on AMZN/JPM):
+
+- Candidate segment medians are **unchanged** across zero/realistic/stress2x at
+  every lookback (universe median +0.069; positive-edge assets 6/6/6 at lookback
+  3, 6/6/6 at lookback 5, 5/6/6 at lookback 10). Mechanical classification:
+  **COST_ROBUST** at every lookback.
+- **But this robustness is definitional, not evidentiary**: a non-flipping
+  (static/level) position pays almost no turnover cost. Full-sample active sign
+  flips are 0 for 9/10 tickers (NVDA 1); realistic-cost commission is only
+  ~0.9–4.7% of capital over the full sample for 9 tickers. A genuine
+  daily-rebalanced momentum strategy would flip sign frequently and show material
+  cost sensitivity; the observed near-zero sensitivity is itself the tell that no
+  momentum signal is present.
+- Methodological caveat (recorded): the coin-flip null churns and therefore pays
+  costs, so some candidate-vs-null **verdict** shifts under cost (e.g. JPM
+  lookback 5: zero=REGIME_DEPENDENT → realistic/stress2x=REGIME_STABLE; lookback
+  3 REGIME_DEPENDENT count 2 → 1) are null-dispersion artifacts, not changes in
+  the candidate medians.
+
+**Independent verification.** `research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`
+(fresh `walk_forward`/`noise_benchmark`, not `stress_segments`) MATCHed: the
+signal-definition diagnostic (AAPL/AMZN/NVDA/JPM/XOM × lookbacks 3/5/10); AMZN/JPM
+candidate medians + null medians + regenerated verdicts for all 9 lookback×cost
+cells; universe medians + positive-edge counts; determinism. Regression suite
+168/168 pass. The check artifact is byte-identical across two independent full runs
+(sha256 `71cb1e6478fc143e2ce95afcd242bedbbf1f4ee5c7d51bbc51d20b7a3dc23c49`).
+
+**Verdict: CONFOUNDED / VERIFIED_NEGATIVE_RESULT.** There is no genuine momentum
+edge in the current implementation to be cost-tested. The qualified momentum
+evidence (prior SUPPORTED verdict, activation 37318950814; lookback/horizon
+robustness, 37361000967 / 37394344201) is re-characterized as a **price-level /
+static-long artifact** and is provisional until a corrected lookback-return
+signal is tested. Durable negative finding recorded; the prior positive verdict is
+not erased but is flagged as confounded. Note: `mean_reversion_signals` uses the
+identical mean-log-price formula with the opposite sign, so the reversal class is
+presumed always-short for these tickers and its FALSIFIED verdict is likewise
+provisional (candidate task R-007).
+
+Next action: correct `momentum_signals` to the lookback-return rule and re-run the
+momentum evidence base through the full gate stack (candidate task R-006).
+
+---
+
